{"id":"6.5.2","doc":"T","title":"Functional Description","words":338,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Some of the 256 output signals (signals with a name assigned in the column \"Output signal\" in Table 6.11-1) can be set to go through GPIO matrix into IO MUX and then to a pin."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Figure 6.3-1 illustrates the configuration."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"To output peripheral signal "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Y"}]},{"t":"text","v":" to a particular GPIO pin "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"X"}]},{"t":"text","v":" (see notes 1 and 2 below), follow these steps:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Configure GPIO_FUNC"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":"_OUT_SEL_CFG_REG and "},{"t":"reg","v":"GPIO_ENABLE_REG"},{"t":"text","v":"["},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":"] corresponding to GPIO pin "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"X"}]},{"t":"text","v":" in GPIO matrix."}]},{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Recommended operation: use corresponding W1TS (write 1 to set) and W1TC (write 1 to clear) registers to set or clear "},{"t":"reg","v":"GPIO_ENABLE_REG"},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Set the GPIO_FUNC"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":"_OUT_SEL field in register GPIO_FUNC"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":"_OUT_SEL_CFG_REG to the index of the desired peripheral output signal "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Y"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"If the signal should always be enabled as an output, set the bit GPIO_FUNC"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":"_OEN_SEL in register GPIO_FUNC"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":"_OUT_SEL_CFG_REG and the bit in register GPIO_ENABLE/"},{"t":"reg","v":"ENABLE1_W1TS_REG"},{"t":"text",